{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261118T190904Z-b3ff674b", "ts": "2026-11-18T19:12:23Z", "actor": {"worktree": ".claude/worktrees/server-image", "plugin": "3.8.2-dev.1", "branch": "fix/server-image-test-target", "build": "3682719168c6"}, "body": {"base_commit": "e7aea5303a483d4c6f88e2f8b17d20034d78567a", "base_tree": "3dde361afc8b5a54f0f1798fa014bf6e1f013fe0", "head_tree": "5da22dd3f906fe45fd9bd200b939cb1fad05dabf", "head_commit": "ebc7763e481354864d09b3a777d65a5184a1df59", "dispatch_commit": "ebc7763e481354864d09b3a777d65a5184a1df59", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": [".devcontainer/Dockerfile", ".github/workflows/suites.yml", "arrt/Dockerfile", "arrt/tests/unit/test_wall_state_words.py", "deploy/README.md"], "files_changed": [".devcontainer/Dockerfile", ".github/workflows/suites.yml", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-server-image.md", ".prawduct/changes/server-image.md", "arrt/Dockerfile", "arrt/tests/unit/test_wall_state_words.py", "deploy/README.md"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-server-image.md", ".prawduct/changes/server-image.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "The image leg's pytest ignore set is a hand-kept second copy that no derived guard checks", "recommendation": "Scope: class. It broke because the new leg's pytest invocation lives in arrt/Dockerfile (`--ignore=tests/browser`, line 100), and every guard that holds a CI pytest invocation only scans .github/workflows. `tests/test_default_suite_ci_scope.py` derives the ignore set from `importorskip` calls and checks it in both directions, but only for the suites.yml `arrt` job, and the suites.yml comment says 'The ignore set is not maintained by hand'. The image job feeds the same `assert_tests_ran.py`, which treats any skip as a provisioning failure. So when someone adds a directory that calls `importorskip` (the guard's own example is `tests/perf/`), the guard sends them to the curation line in suites.yml, and the image job then fails with 'skipped in CI ... a dependency was not provisioned'. That is the false alarm the guard was written to prevent. In the other direction, an ignore left behind in the Dockerfile silently drops a directory from the image run. Per the learning 'When code is added, moved or retired, ask which guards were scoped to the old shape or to where you looked, and carry them to the surviving code', fix it by construction: have `test_default_suite_ci_scope.py` also read the pytest RUN line of the Dockerfile's `test` stage, as the `image` leg, and call `check_ignores(..., needed)` on it. The bound to search: every pytest invocation that writes a report `assert_tests_ran.py` reads but sits outside .github/workflows. Today that is only arrt/Dockerfile.", "files": ["arrt/Dockerfile", ".github/workflows/suites.yml"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "warning", "title": "image job reports a red suite as 'pytest never produced a report'", "recommendation": "Instance. In the `image` job, the 'Fail if nothing actually ran' step carries `if: always()`, copied from the sibling jobs. There, a missing report means pytest never ran. Here, the test stage's RUN fails on any red test, so `test-report` is never exported and `image-report/results.xml` is missing. assert_tests_ran.py then prints `::error::image-report/results.xml does not exist \u2014 pytest never produced a report`, and its own comment says this means 'a collection error, a bad marker expression, or an install that did not complete'. On the most common failure, a failing test, the job's clearest annotation sends the person on call looking for a provisioning or collection fault, and the failing test ids are only in the buildx log. Per the learning 'When a check can be quiet for more than one reason, give each quiet state its own output', give the two causes of a missing report their own outputs. The simplest fix is to run the step only when the build step succeeded (give it an `id` and use `if: steps.<id>.outcome == 'success'`), so a red build reports only the build's own error. The alternative is to let the stage always export the report together with pytest's exit status and fail on that status. Either way, re-break a test once and check that the annotation names the right cause.", "files": [".github/workflows/suites.yml", "arrt/Dockerfile"], "fid": "R-2"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 2, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "The image's pytest --ignore set is outside the guard that derives the curation leg's", "recommendation": "tests/test_default_suite_ci_scope.py derives the curation leg's --ignore set from the tree, but it reads only `uv run ... pytest` lines in suites.yml. The new invocation's `--ignore=tests/browser` lives in arrt/Dockerfile, where no guard sees it. Learnings rule: 'When code is added, moved or retired, ask which guards were scoped to the old shape or to where you looked, and carry them to the surviving code'. Today either kind of drift fails loudly or does no harm. A new importorskip directory makes the image job red, naming the skip, and if tests/browser ever imports cleanly its tests are deselected by addopts' marker anyway. So no fix is owed now. If a second ignore entry ever appears, extend `_ignored_by` to read the Dockerfile's RUN line as well (class: every pytest invocation outside suites.yml).", "files": ["arrt/Dockerfile"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "The plan has no governed_by field, though the product carries Direction sections", "recommendation": "build-plan-server-image.md declares no `governed_by:`, while architecture.md, nonfunctional-requirements.md, security-model.md and others carry `## Direction`, and sibling plans declare one. So the Governing-Artifact Reconciliation had no disposition to check. I read the norms that bear on this change myself. The project-preferences rule 'Do not add a Node toolchain or a build step for the shipped client' is not breached: only the node binary goes in, it is in the test stage only, there is no build step, and it is the same pin as .devcontainer/Dockerfile. The 'one uv' row is held by test_one_python.py, which is green in evidence. Consider seeding the plan with `prawduct-hook jurisdiction`.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-server-image.md"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "The plan's Goals section has no Response taken line and no Level", "recommendation": "methodology/planning.md's Goals asks for a Response taken line and a Level. This plan has Goals and marked inferences but neither of those. It is an oracle record and clears no Records Pass bar, so this is noted for the next plan rather than owed an edit.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-server-image.md"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "The Node pin's match with the testament image rests on a comment; the uv pin's has a test", "recommendation": "arrt/Dockerfile lines 23-26 say Node is 'pinned as the testament image pins it', and the digest is copied from .devcontainer/Dockerfile. The uv pin across every tracked Dockerfile is held by `tests/test_one_python.py::test_every_image_in_the_tree_runs_the_uv_the_deploy_image_runs`; nothing holds the node pin. Drift would show up as a red run, not a silent pass: the node tests skip only when node is missing, and an older node fails `node --check`. Cheap to carry into the next commit: extend that test, or add one beside it, so every Dockerfile's `FROM node:` matches.", "files": ["arrt/Dockerfile", ".devcontainer/Dockerfile"], "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "The test stage's user is a second literal 568:568 kept equal to the app stage's by a comment", "recommendation": "`USER 568:568` now appears in both the `test` stage and the `app` stage, and the test stage's comment says it is 'the app stage's user'. A single `ARG APP_UID=568` used by both would make it one value. Low stakes: the property the test stage needs is 'unprivileged', and a different uid still has it.", "files": ["arrt/Dockerfile"], "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": ".devcontainer/Dockerfile lists three node-using test modules; there are four", "recommendation": "Lines 13-16 name test_client_vocabulary.py, test_ages.py and test_one_date_formatter.py. arrt/tests/unit/test_route_parsing.py also runs node, and the change record counts four. Nothing reads this list, and the stale part predates this change, though the file is in the diff. If it is ever touched, make it relational ('the curation tests that run the client's modules with node') rather than adding the fourth name. No edit wanted now.", "files": [".devcontainer/Dockerfile"], "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "the Node pin's 'as the testament image pins it' has no guard", "recommendation": "arrt/Dockerfile:23-26 copies the node:22 digest from .devcontainer/Dockerfile and claims the two agree. Nothing checks that. tests/test_one_python.py::test_every_image_in_the_tree_runs_the_uv_the_deploy_image_runs holds the uv pin across every tracked Dockerfile, and the same shape would hold this one. Bumping only the pool's Node fails loudly in the image job's JS tests, so this is an observation. Separately, the header at line 4 lists node among the images the NAS build pins, but node is used only in the test stage.", "files": ["arrt/Dockerfile"], "oid": "O-7"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "the image leg's --ignore is outside the CI-scope guard", "recommendation": "tests/test_default_suite_ci_scope.py derives every suites.yml job's `--ignore` set from the tree in both directions, and its docstring calls over-exclusion 'the one worth a mechanism'. The image leg's `--ignore=tests/browser` lives in arrt/Dockerfile:100, which that guard never reads. Under-exclusion still shows up, because assert_tests_ran fails the job on a skip. A stale extra ignore would quietly shrink what the image runs. Low exposure today, since browser.yml runs tests/browser.", "files": ["arrt/Dockerfile"], "oid": "O-8"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "new CI actions with no recorded why", "recommendation": "docker/setup-buildx-action@v3 and docker/build-push-action@v6 are the repo's first Docker actions. They are tag-pinned like their siblings, and the plan and change record give no reason for them. They are the standard way to get the `type=gha` cache, and no reasonable alternative changes anything, so no edit is wanted.", "files": [".github/workflows/suites.yml"], "oid": "O-9"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "the layer cache may evict the other jobs' uv caches", "recommendation": "`cache-to: type=gha,mode=max` stores the Python install and both environments for each branch. GitHub manages its lifetime (10 GB per repository, LRU eviction, 7 days), so it is not unmanaged. It does share that budget with the setup-uv caches. If uv jobs slow down, look here first.", "files": [".github/workflows/suites.yml"], "oid": "O-10"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "Records Pass: build-plan-server-image.md and changes/server-image.md, no finding", "recommendation": "Covered both files in files_oracle. Checked against the diff: four Node-gated test modules (test_ages, test_client_vocabulary, test_one_date_formatter, test_route_parsing), tools/ copied, USER 568:568, STATIC_DIR, the tests/browser ignore matching the curation job, the digest matching .devcontainer, and the app stage unchanged with app still the last (default) stage. None clears a bar. Below the bars: the change record says deploy/README.md says the image is amd64-only, but the README only implies it (the --platform command and 'under emulation on an arm Mac'). It does not say a native arm64 build fails at the dezoomify-rs step, or why. The plan's chunk 'What' does not mention the Node copy or the test-report stage that the change record does. No edit wanted.", "files": [".prawduct/changes/server-image.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-server-image.md"], "oid": "O-11"}], "duration_seconds": 420, "scope": "server-image", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": ["01"], "chunks_proposed": [], "base_reviewed": "e7aea5303a483d4c6f88e2f8b17d20034d78567a", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-server-image.md", ".prawduct/changes/server-image.md", "deploy/README.md"], "chunk_graded": "01", "chunks_graded": ["01"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-server-image.md", "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 0, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "span": "full", "bounded_from": null, "span_reason": "base-moved", "dispatched_at": "2026-11-18T19:09:04Z"}}

